#HTML^<p>Kentilla is driven from Sinclair BASIC with a machine-code support
layer for input, graphics and helpers. This page is a <code>LIST</code> of
the tokenised program in the post-load snapshot (870 lines), from
<code>PROG</code> at #R$5CCB up to <code>VARS</code> at #R$E56B.</p>
<p>The command loop at line 113 prints <code>What now?</code> then enters
the support code with <code>LET A=USR</code> #R$EA66 and
<code>LET A=USR</code> #R$EA6C. Verb and noun indices come back through
#R$EA60 / #R$EA63 / #R$EA6F and are dispatched with
<code>GO TO n*100+1000</code> / <code>GO SUB 1000</code>. Location text
lives in the high line numbers (9900s).</p>
<pre class="basic" style="white-space:pre; overflow:auto; font-size:12px; line-height:1.35">
